  "sources": {
    "decisions-md:2026-11-02": "agents/DECISIONS.md [2026-11-02] records the applied sequence IOS_DEVICE_ONLY_MODE=true then CLOUD_RENDER_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false. Production jobs carry assembly_plan.native_device_only=true, which agrees. A repo statement, no secret read.",
    "default": "Code default. Production may override it through a Fly secret that was not read; treat the value as unconfirmed.",
    "job-data:creator_brief_binding-2026-11-14": "Every sampled production creation job from 2026-11-04 to 2026-11-13 (6 of 6, two accounts) carries assembly_plan.creator_brief_binding, which only the writer cohort produces. Whether production uses the global flag or an allowlist is not known; the replay user is synthetic, so the global flag is the approximation. Read with admin GET /admin/jobs/<id>/debug.",
    "job-data:no-semantic-planner-2026-11-14": "No nova.plan.semantic_edit_proposal or nova.plan.edit_proposal agent run appears in GET /admin/plan-items/<id>/proposal-trace for the 30 plan items behind the 60 most recent production content-plan jobs (2026-10-28..2026-11-14, 11 failed and 40+ finished jobs), and CLAUDE.md lists EDIT_PROPOSAL_SEMANTIC_ENABLED as false. Supersedes the 2026-10-08 Fly digest comparison, which read it as on (changed since, or never reached on this route).",
    "legacy-fly-digest-2026-10-08": "Boolean flags that shared PHONE_RENDERING_ENABLED's Fly secret digest (last re-derived 2026-10-08 into the former hand list in tests/_prod_profile.py). Digests were compared, no value was read. Flags enabled after that date are not recorded here.",
    "live:phone-render-config": "GET /admin/kria/phone-render-config on the production API (names only, no secret value); re-read on every `refresh --live`.",
    "reconciled:edit-wide-looks-2026-11-14": "CLAUDE.md lists EDIT_WIDE_LOOKS_ENABLED as off, but that line was written when the feature shipped dark (#857, 2026-08-18) and describes the code default. On 2026-10-08 the Fly secret shared PHONE_RENDERING_ENABLED's digest (an equal value, true). No later record turns it off, so the newer production observation is kept. A doc line outranks an observation only when it records a change applied after it (as the 2026-11-14 job data does for EDIT_PROPOSAL_SEMANTIC_ENABLED).",
    "runbook:chat-speech-cleanup-rollout": "docs/runbooks/chat-speech-cleanup-rollout.md says the retake switches have been on in prod since 2026-11-04. A repo statement, no secret read."
  }
}
